-tip testing found a different crash, there's a spontaneous 
reboot somewhere during user-space startup:

[   17.454891] EXT3-fs: mounted filesystem with ordered data mode.
[   19.488369] eth0: no link during initialization.
[   22.023754] eth0: link up.
[   24.366361] Adding 3911816k swap on /dev/sda2.  Priority:-1 extents:1 across:3911816k 

It just reboots after that point. When i exclude the cpus4096 
changes it continues with:

[   25.354866] ssh used greatest stack depth: 1564 bytes left                       
[   25.783102] Unmapping cpu 1 from all nodes                                       
[   25.784650] CPU 1 is now offline                                                 

Note, it might have crashed in a cpu hotplug test i'm conducting 
during bootup:

echo 0 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online
sleep 1
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online
sleep 1
echo 0 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online
sleep 1
echo 1 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online

Config attached. (you need to run it through 'make oldconfig')

	Ingo

